   "id": 616226,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<figure id=\"fig06\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/0d5c878bdc2d5e98.png\" alt=\"The map is titled “Air Attack of Oahu.” A first wave lists 49 level bombers, 51 dive bombers, 40 torpedo bombers, and 43 fighters. Arrows come from the first wave; one arrow of dive bombers goes to Wheeler Field. The rest of the first wave goes to Pearl Harbor. The second wave lists 54 level bombers, 78 dive bombers, and 35 fighters. One arrow heads to Kaneohe field, and the rest head to Pearl Harbor.\">\n<figcaption>Note that dates and times of the Japanese fleet location are given as Tokyo time, not local time (for example, December 8 is December 7 local time in Hawaii, and 0310 (3:10 a.m.) is 0740 (7:40 a.m. local time).</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the map provided.</i></p>\n<p>The events depicted in the map directly led to</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1172872,
     "content_html": "President Franklin Roosevelt’s referring to this as “a date which will live in infamy”"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172871,
     "content_html": "the unconditional surrender of Germany and Japan"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172870,
     "content_html": "American acquisition of the Philippines"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172869,
     "content_html": "American support of the League of Nations"
    }
   ],
